    "id": "post:practice:vedanta-sakshi-practice",
    "kind": "post",
    "title": "Sakshi Bhav \u2014 Vedanta Ki Woh Practice Jo 10 Second Mein Ho",
    "body": "Abhi \u2014 kuch feel ho raha hai tumhe?\n\nChahe anxiety ho, frustration, ya sirf ek background restlessness \u2014 notice karo ki tum andar se us cheez ke saath merge ho gaye ho ya nahi.\n\n'Main anxious hoon' \u2014 is sentence mein tum anxiety ho.\n\nAb sirf words badlo: 'Main anxiety ko dekh raha hoon.'\n\nYeh sirf reframing nahi hai. Yeh ek genuinely alag neural position hai.\n\nPehle sentence mein koi observer nahi hai \u2014 sirf experience hai. Doosre sentence mein observer exist karta hai. Woh observer \u2014 Vedanta mein \u2014 tumhara actual swaroop hai. Sakshi. Witness.\n\nAur yahi psychologically bhi hota hai \u2014 jab emotion ko observe karte ho, prefrontal cortex activate hota hai, amygdala ki reactivity thodi kam hoti hai. Sirf naming se.\n\nYeh detachment nahi hai. Yeh zyaada complete presence hai \u2014 feel bhi kar rahe ho, aur dub bhi nahi rahe.\n\nAaj practice karo \u2014 jab bhi koi strong emotion aaye: 'Main yeh feel kar raha hoon.' Observer ne notice kiya. Woh observer tum ho.",
